[{:db/id 17592186231570 :question/problem "A particle of mass $0.5\\,\\text{kg}$ is attached to a massless spring. An external periodic force \n\n$$\nF(t)=(3{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)-\\frac{3}{2})\\,\\text{N}\n$$\n\nis applied to the particle.\n\nThe position of the particle is $y(t)$ (measured in meters), and $t>0$ is the time in seconds. If the particle moves with forced harmonic motion without damping and the system experiences resonance, what is the spring constant $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}${\\text{kg/s}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of motion for a particle of mass $m$ moving with forced harmonic motion without damping under the action of a spring with spring constant $k$ and external force $F(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nm{y}^{″}=-ky+F(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $m$ and $F(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n0.5{y}^{″}=-ky+(3{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)-\\frac{3}{2}).\n$$\n\nSimplifying and rearranging the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2ky=3(2{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)-1).\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ here represents simple harmonic motion, and it can be written as\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t,\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants of integration, and $\\omega $ is the system's internal frequency.\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=2k\\,⟹\\,k=\\frac{1}{2}{\\omega }^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe oscillator experiences resonance when the frequency of the external periodic force $f(t)=3(2{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)-1)$ is equal to the frequency of the complementary solution $\\omega .$ Since\n\n$$\nf(t)=3(2{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)-1)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t),\n$$\n\nthe frequency of the external periodic force is $4.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{1}{2}{\\omega }^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {4}^{2}=8\\,{\\text{kg/s}}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186230295 :answer-field/correct "answer-498bed50-28c7-50fa-a5df-0080495261c3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-498bed50-28c7-50fa-a5df-0080495261c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-498bed50-28c7-50fa-a5df-0080495261c3" :answer/id #uuid "498bed50-28c7-50fa-a5df-0080495261c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316816 :answer-field/correct "answer-282a52cc-8658-5a56-b555-abd92b1826a5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-282a52cc-8658-5a56-b555-abd92b1826a5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-282a52cc-8658-5a56-b555-abd92b1826a5" :answer/id #uuid "282a52cc-8658-5a56-b555-abd92b1826a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186317429 :question/problem "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The particle is acted on by an external periodic force\n$f(t)=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t).$\nAssuming the system experiences resonance, which of the following could be used to represent the general solution for the position $y(t)?$\n\nI. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t+ϕ)+\\frac{5}{8}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)$\n\nII. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t+ϕ)+\\frac{5}{8}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)$\n\nIII. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)-\\frac{5}{8}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R,$ and $ϕ$ are constants." :question/worked-solution "Because the motion is undamped and the system experiences resonance, the forcing frequency equals the natural frequency $\\omega .$\n\nThe external force is $f(t)=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t),$ which is sinusoidal with frequency $4.$ Therefore,\n$\\omega =4.$\n\nThe complementary solution for the associated simple harmonic motion equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n1\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t+ϕ)$\n\n2\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t+ϕ)$\n\n3\\. ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)$\n\nAt resonance, a sinusoidal trial at frequency $\\omega $ duplicates the complementary solution, so we multiply by $t$ and take a resonant particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)).\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution and $\\omega =4$ into the differential equation, ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[16(D-Ct)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-16(C+Dt)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)]+16t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)) & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ 16D\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-16C\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients, $C=0$ and $D=\\frac{5}{8}.$ \n\nSo, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\frac{5}{8}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t).\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n1\\. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t+ϕ)+\\frac{5}{8}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)$\n\n2\\. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t+ϕ)+\\frac{5}{8}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)$\n\n3\\. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+\\frac{5}{8}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)$\n\nOnly solution II matches the forms above.\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-14d1651e-04e2-5488-8374-7db989fc704e" :activity/id #uuid "14d1651e-04e2-5488-8374-7db989fc704e" :activity/title "Resonance in Vibrating Systems" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048966 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-2595439f-c010-51c2-987d-b6e986cd13da" "step-77f21bd5-7692-5988-9811-98041bd1e682" "step-2c212f16-03c8-5837-8c98-8164c674583d" "step-de131a05-d058-5098-9651-430e6d375558" "step-c0f6cdf0-cd51-5bdc-9771-44211b216c7d"] :activity/first-step "step-2595439f-c010-51c2-987d-b6e986cd13da" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-2595439f-c010-51c2-987d-b6e986cd13da" :step/id #uuid "2595439f-c010-51c2-987d-b6e986cd13da" :step/content 17592186231567 :step/next "step-77f21bd5-7692-5988-9811-98041bd1e682" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-77f21bd5-7692-5988-9811-98041bd1e682" :step/id #uuid "77f21bd5-7692-5988-9811-98041bd1e682" :step/content 17592186231570 :step/next "step-2c212f16-03c8-5837-8c98-8164c674583d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2c212f16-03c8-5837-8c98-8164c674583d" :step/id #uuid "2c212f16-03c8-5837-8c98-8164c674583d" :step/content 17592186317422 :step/next "step-de131a05-d058-5098-9651-430e6d375558" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-de131a05-d058-5098-9651-430e6d375558" :step/id #uuid "de131a05-d058-5098-9651-430e6d375558" :step/content 17592186317429 :step/next "step-c0f6cdf0-cd51-5bdc-9771-44211b216c7d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c0f6cdf0-cd51-5bdc-9771-44211b216c7d" :step/id #uuid "c0f6cdf0-cd51-5bdc-9771-44211b216c7d" :step/content 17592186427272 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
